  "notes": "West's club opening lead goes to South's ♣A. South has 2 inescapable heart losers and could lose 2 diamonds tricks if West has 4 diamonds to the ♦Q.\n\nBy playing for an elimination, South can guarantee the contract. South should draw trump and play a diamond to dummy. Dummy's second club is ruffed and South exits in hearts.\n\nA diamond play from either defender allows South to play that suit for 1 loser regardless of how diamonds lie. As a club return yields a ruff and discard, the defense must continue hearts.\n\nSouth ruffs and plays a low diamond. When West follows small, South should duck in dummy. If East can win this trick, diamonds are breaking. If East discards, West is endplayed. He must either lead a diamond away from the ♦Q or give a ruff and discard by leading clubs.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West's club opening lead goes to South's ♣A. South has 2 inescapable heart losers and could lose 2 diamonds tricks if West has 4 diamonds to the ♦Q.",
